      'Hearing turns tiny vibrations of the air into nerve signals. The ear can detect sounds from about 20 to 20,000 vibrations per second (hertz). It has three parts, each with a job: the outer ear collects sound, the middle ear transfers it, and the inner ear converts it into nerve signals. The inner ear also contains the organs of balance.',
